(37,'[\"Identify unsanitized output rendered in the browser for Stored XSS Awareness\",\"Inject and execute malicious scripts in victim context\",\"Understand impact on other users and session hijacking\",\"Apply output encoding and CSP as countermeasures\"]','[\"A community forum platform allows users to post comments visible to all members.\",\"The application renders user-submitted content without sufficient sanitization, exposing it to Stored XSS Awareness.\",\"An admin reviews new posts periodically, making their session a high-value target.\",\"Your goal is to inject a payload that executes in the victim\'s browser and captures the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Try a simple <script>alert(1)</script> first to confirm execution.\",\"Look for unsanitized reflection in the page source.\",\"Consider stored context — does your payload persist after a page reload?\"]','[{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/\",\"title\":\"OWASP XSS Overview\"},{\"sub\":\"cheatsheetseries.owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html\",\"title\":\"OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet\"},{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/cross-site-scripting\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – XSS\"}]'),
