(53,'[\"Identify insecure API design patterns related to API Parameter Pollution Awareness\",\"Exploit authorization, exposure, or parameter issues\",\"Retrieve sensitive data or perform unauthorized actions\",\"Apply API security best practices and rate limiting\"]','[\"A logistics company recently launched a REST API to integrate with third-party partners.\",\"The API was built quickly with a focus on features, leaving it vulnerable to API Parameter Pollution Awareness.\",\"You have obtained a valid low-privilege API token through their public developer portal.\",\"Your mission is to exploit the API security flaw and access data beyond your authorization scope.\"]','[\"Intercept API calls and look for IDs or object references you can manipulate.\",\"Are there fields in the response you can try sending back in a write request?\",\"Check if the API uses numeric sequential IDs — can you enumerate them?\"]','[{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-api-security/\",\"title\":\"OWASP API Security Top 10\"},{\"sub\":\"cheatsheetseries.owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/REST_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html\",\"title\":\"OWASP REST Security Cheat Sheet\"},{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/api-testing\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – API Testing\"}]'),
(54,'[\"Identify insecure API design patterns related to GraphQL Introspection Awareness\",\"Exploit authorization, exposure, or parameter issues\",\"Retrieve sensitive data or perform unauthorized actions\",\"Apply API security best practices and rate limiting\"]','[\"A logistics company recently launched a REST API to integrate with third-party partners.\",\"The API was built quickly with a focus on features, leaving it vulnerable to GraphQL Introspection Awareness.\",\"You have obtained a valid low-privilege API token through their public developer portal.\",\"Your mission is to exploit the API security flaw and access data beyond your authorization scope.\"]','[\"Intercept API calls and look for IDs or object references you can manipulate.\",\"Are there fields in the response you can try sending back in a write request?\",\"Check if the API uses numeric sequential IDs — can you enumerate them?\"]','[{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-api-security/\",\"title\":\"OWASP API Security Top 10\"},{\"sub\":\"cheatsheetseries.owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/REST_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html\",\"title\":\"OWASP REST Security Cheat Sheet\"},{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/api-testing\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – API Testing\"}]'),
(55,'[\"Identify implicit assumptions in business workflows for Payment Validation Logic Scenario\",\"Manipulate requests to break intended logic\",\"Achieve unauthorized outcomes such as price or flow bypass\",\"Understand testing techniques for logic flaws\"]','[\"An online retailer runs a discount and transaction system for promotional campaigns.\",\"The checkout flow was designed without adversarial testing, leading to Payment Validation Logic Scenario.\",\"Assumptions baked into server-side logic may allow manipulation of prices or workflow steps.\",\"Your task is to identify the logic flaw, exploit it, and retrieve the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Try submitting negative or zero values for prices or quantities.\",\"What assumptions does the workflow make about request ordering?\",\"Repeat a request that should only succeed once.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/logic-flaws\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – Business Logic Vulnerabilities\"},{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/10-Business_Logic_Testing\",\"title\":\"OWASP Testing Guide – Business Logic\"}]'),
(56,'[\"Identify implicit assumptions in business workflows for Race Condition Awareness\",\"Manipulate requests to break intended logic\",\"Achieve unauthorized outcomes such as price or flow bypass\",\"Understand testing techniques for logic flaws\"]','[\"An online retailer runs a discount and transaction system for promotional campaigns.\",\"The checkout flow was designed without adversarial testing, leading to Race Condition Awareness.\",\"Assumptions baked into server-side logic may allow manipulation of prices or workflow steps.\",\"Your task is to identify the logic flaw, exploit it, and retrieve the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Try submitting negative or zero values for prices or quantities.\",\"What assumptions does the workflow make about request ordering?\",\"Repeat a request that should only succeed once.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/logic-flaws\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – Business Logic Vulnerabilities\"},{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/10-Business_Logic_Testing\",\"title\":\"OWASP Testing Guide – Business Logic\"}]'),
(57,'[\"Identify implicit assumptions in business workflows for Price Manipulation Logic Scenario\",\"Manipulate requests to break intended logic\",\"Achieve unauthorized outcomes such as price or flow bypass\",\"Understand testing techniques for logic flaws\"]','[\"An online retailer runs a discount and transaction system for promotional campaigns.\",\"The checkout flow was designed without adversarial testing, leading to Price Manipulation Logic Scenario.\",\"Assumptions baked into server-side logic may allow manipulation of prices or workflow steps.\",\"Your task is to identify the logic flaw, exploit it, and retrieve the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Try submitting negative or zero values for prices or quantities.\",\"What assumptions does the workflow make about request ordering?\",\"Repeat a request that should only succeed once.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/logic-flaws\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – Business Logic Vulnerabilities\"},{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/10-Business_Logic_Testing\",\"title\":\"OWASP Testing Guide – Business Logic\"}]'),
(58,'[\"Identify implicit assumptions in business workflows for Coupon Validation Scenario\",\"Manipulate requests to break intended logic\",\"Achieve unauthorized outcomes such as price or flow bypass\",\"Understand testing techniques for logic flaws\"]','[\"An online retailer runs a discount and transaction system for promotional campaigns.\",\"The checkout flow was designed without adversarial testing, leading to Coupon Validation Scenario.\",\"Assumptions baked into server-side logic may allow manipulation of prices or workflow steps.\",\"Your task is to identify the logic flaw, exploit it, and retrieve the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Try submitting negative or zero values for prices or quantities.\",\"What assumptions does the workflow make about request ordering?\",\"Repeat a request that should only succeed once.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"portswigger.net\",\"href\":\"https://portswigger.net/web-security/logic-flaws\",\"title\":\"PortSwigger – Business Logic Vulnerabilities\"},{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/latest/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/10-Business_Logic_Testing\",\"title\":\"OWASP Testing Guide – Business Logic\"}]'),
(59,'[\"Understand dependency management risks in the context of Dependency Management Security Scenario\",\"Identify attack vectors in third-party packages\",\"Recognize typosquatting and confusion attack patterns\",\"Apply secure dependency hygiene practices\"]','[\"A technology company has onboarded you to review their CI/CD pipeline and dependency management.\",\"They rely on dozens of open-source packages, exposing them to Dependency Management Security Scenario.\",\"The build system automatically installs packages without lockfile enforcement in some stages.\",\"Your objective is to identify the supply chain vulnerability and locate the hidden flag.\"]','[\"Check package names for slight misspellings compared to popular libraries.\",\"Look at what version constraints are set in the manifest file.\",\"Check if there is a lockfile and whether it is enforced during CI.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"owasp.org\",\"href\":\"https://owasp.org/www-project-scvs/\",\"title\":\"OWASP Software Component Verification Standard\"},{\"sub\":\"attack.mitre.org\",\"href\":\"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1195/\",\"title\":\"MITRE ATT&CK – Supply Chain Compromise\"}]'),
(60,'[\"Identify exposed assets and dangling references related to Subdomain Takeover Awareness\",\"Enumerate subdomains and misconfigured cloud resources\",\"Understand subdomain takeover preconditions\",\"Apply defensive DNS and asset management practices\"]','[\"A fintech company is concerned about their external attack surface after a competitor suffered a breach.\",\"During preliminary recon you discover an asset vulnerable to Subdomain Takeover Awareness.\",\"A DNS record was never cleaned up after a legacy system was retired six months ago.\",\"Your goal is to demonstrate the risk and retrieve the hidden flag as proof of concept.\"]','[\"Look up the subdomain or asset in public DNS / certificate transparency records.\",\"Check whether the cloud resource it points to is still claimed.\",\"Try visiting the asset directly in your browser.\"]','[{\"sub\":\"hackerone.com\",\"href\":\"https://www.hackerone.com/application-security/guide-subdomain-takeovers\",\"title\":\"HackerOne – Subdomain Takeover\"},{\"sub\":\"github.com\",\"href\":\"https://github.com/EdOverflow/can-i-take-over-xyz\",\"title\":\"can-i-take-over-xyz\"}]');